ant user you can run the gcloud add  iem policy binding command  next let's set up a service account that  will be associated with the connector vm  start by uploading policy for cloud  manager version  gcp.yml permission file to the cloud  shell  then go to iem and admin  navigate to service account  then create a new service account  for a service account name choose netapp  connector  for role choose netapp cloud central  now we have a google cloud user with the  permissions required to create a  connector from cod manager  as well as a service account for the  connector vm let's enable cloud api  needed for cloud volumes go to api and  service tab  we'll need to make sure the following  apis are enabled  cloud deployment manager v2 api  cloud logging api  cloud resource manager api  compute engine api  identity and access management iem api  now let's deploy netapp first go to the  marketplace  cloud volumes landing page and choose  manage on provider  create an account or walk into your  existing account  next we'll navigate to fabric view  and choose cod volumes on tap  go to cloud manager  let's add our first working environment  first we'll choose google cloud platform  next we'll choose cloud volumes on tap  now let's create a connector which  allows cloud manager to manage resources  and processes within your public cloud  environment we'll choose google cloud  platform we will need to provide  permissions to connect our google  account with cloud manager  we'll set our connector instance name  let's use test connector  we'll set the project it will be  connected to test ctd  we'll set service account netapp  connector  next we'll set the location details i'll  keep the defaults  then we'll set the connectivity to  public ip enable  and finally for the firewall policy  choose my ip  now that we filled out all this  additional information make sure to  review the details  as you can see the connector was  successfully created congratulations on  successfully deploying a netapp cloud  volumes on tap instance you now have a  platform to simplify the management of  your workloads on google cloud  if you enjoyed this video please  subscribe and hit the like button below  we encourage you to check out the google  cloud marketplace and deploy the  solution on your own thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

